# ─── Secrets & credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing in these patterns should EVER reach a commit. If a secret is
# ever committed, rotating the credential is mandatory — deleting the
# file does not remove it from git history.
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.ppk
*.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.*
credentials.*
*credential*
*password*
*apikey*
*api_key*
*api-keys*
*API Keys*
# NOTE: *token* is intentionally over-broad. It will also exclude innocent files
# like auth-token-notes.md. Over-exclusion is the safe failure mode here -
# add a targeted negation (as below) rather than loosening the pattern.
*token*
!*tokenizer*
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.ovpn
*.kdbx

# ─── Cloud / infrastructure state ────────────────────────────────────
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
.aws/
.azure/
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig

# ─── Lab artifacts that may contain host detail ──────────────────────
# Raw captures and exports routinely embed hostnames, internal IPs,
# usernames and MAC addresses. Sanitised excerpts go in the writeup;
# raw files stay local.
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.evtx
*.etl
*.dmp
*.mem
raw/
_private/
_unsanitised/

# ─── OS & editor noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ─── Build & dependency output ───────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
bin/
obj/
dist/
build/
